# Randomized cross-language differential conformance suite.
# Produced 2026-09-01 on windows/amd64, Go go1.26.5, Python 3.12.10.
#
# Go side generates 2000 randomized VALID cases from a fixed master seed
# (dfrl-agg/differential_test.go) and writes vectors/differential.json in the
# same schema as the nine curated vectors. The independent Python reference
# (pyref/, zero shared code, zero shared dependencies) recomputes every root.

=== curated (9) ===
------------------------------------------------------------------------
9/9 cases byte-identical across Go and Python

=== randomized (2000) ===
------------------------------------------------------------------------
2000/2000 cases byte-identical across Go and Python

=== MUTATION SENSITIVITY ===
# A suite that cannot fail proves nothing. Injecting ties-away-from-zero in
# place of ties-to-even in the Python reference -- the subtlest deviation the
# rounding rule admits -- was detected as:
#     curated:    5/9 match    (4 caught)
#     randomized: 1738/2000 match (262 caught)
# The reference was restored and re-verified byte-identical to its pristine copy.
